.Dd $Mdocdate: November 24 2026 $
.Dt ANSILOVE_LOADFILE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ansilove_loadfile
.Nd Load a file from disk
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In ansilove.h
.Ft int
.Fn ansilove_loadfile "struct ansilove_ctx *ctx" "const char *input"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn ansilove_loadfile
function opens
.Fa input
for reading and maps its contents into memory.
The context
.Fa ctx
must have been initialized with
.Xr ansilove_init 3 .
.Pp
On success,
.Va ctx->buffer
points to a read-only mapping, and
.Va ctx->maplen
and
.Va ctx->length
contain the file size in bytes.
The file descriptor is closed before the function returns.
An empty file cannot be mapped and causes this function to fail.
.Pp
This function does not detect the file format or render the input.
Call the appropriate rendering function after loading the file.
Release the mapping with
.Xr ansilove_clean 3
before loading another file into the same context.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn ansilove_loadfile
function returns 0 on success and \-1 on failure.
On failure, if
.Fa ctx
is not
.Dv NULL ,
.Va ctx->error
is set to an error code described in
.Xr ansilove_error 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ansilove_clean 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_error 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_init 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_savefile 3 ,
.Xr libansilove 3
